Subject: [PATCH] fix(v45.4.1): align final verify script with the WebView
 formula editor

CI broke on verify_native_final.py because it still read the deleted native
formula editor files (FormulaEditorDialog.kt and friends).

- formula_editor now reads MathEditorWebViewDialog.kt; deleted-file reads and
  their checks (FormulaBoxEditor/FormulaReferenceLibrary/FormulaLibraryDialog/
  FormulaLibraryNavigator/FormulaSmartHubDialog/FormulaSmartReference + native
  library asset + marker lists) removed.
- android.webkit restriction reworked: exactly one file (MathEditorWebViewDialog.kt)
  may import android.webkit.
- New V45.4 checks: math_editor_standalone.html asset (>500KB, contains
  function openMath(targetId) and function mfApply()); dialog is a full-screen
  WebView with AndroidMathBridge; bridge follows the qTxt_1 openMath/mfApply/
  closeMath contract; ExamBuilderScreen uses MathEditorWebViewDialog; no native
  editor remnants in main_text.
- Native rendering checks (SVG/canvas/codec/natural converter, ExistingFormulaEditor)
  kept unchanged.
- Result: FINAL_NATIVE_VERIFY=PASS kotlin_files=168 edge_functions=3
